@startuml UC001_Provider_Login_Sequence
!theme plain
title UC001 — Google or GitHub sign-in with a linked account

actor Browser
participant "src/server.js" as Server
participant "src/routes/auth.routes.js" as Routes
participant "src/routes/oauth.routes.js" as OAuth
participant "src/services/oauthService.js" as ProviderService
participant "Google or GitHub" as Provider
participant "src/services/authService.js" as Auth
participant "src/services/tokenService.js" as Tokens
participant "src/db/database.js" as Data
database PostgreSQL as DB

Browser -> Server : GET /api/oauth/:provider/start
Server -> Routes : Dispatch to /api
Routes -> OAuth : Dispatch to /oauth
OAuth -> ProviderService : beginOAuth()
ProviderService --> OAuth : Provider URL and signed transaction
OAuth --> Browser : Set transaction cookie and redirect
Browser -> Provider : Sign in and authorize
Provider --> Browser : Redirect back with code and state

Browser -> Server : GET /api/oauth/:provider/callback
Server -> Routes : Dispatch to /api
Routes -> OAuth : Dispatch to callback
OAuth -> ProviderService : Validate transaction and retrieve identity
ProviderService -> Provider : Exchange code and request identity
Provider --> ProviderService : Verified provider identity
ProviderService --> OAuth : Provider user ID
OAuth -> Data : findProviderUser()
Data -> DB : Read account linked to provider identity
Data --> OAuth : Account ID
OAuth -> Auth : startSession()
Auth -> Tokens : Generate and hash refresh token
Tokens --> Auth : Refresh token and hash
Auth -> Data : insertSession()
Data -> DB : Save session and refresh token hash
Auth --> OAuth : Session and refresh token
OAuth -> Routes : setRefreshCookie()
OAuth --> Browser : Redirect to app

note over Browser, Routes
  After the redirect, the browser calls POST /api/refresh
  to exchange the refresh cookie for an access token.
end note
@enduml
